# The checkbox, and the first thing in this client that is multi-select.
#
# Settings > Position, under "Sent with a position": ten bits of one protobuf field, drawn as
# ten rows. A square rather than a switch is the whole point of the scene - the rows above the
# heading are settings that act on their own and wear the switch, and the rows below it are
# members of one value, which is the sentence the control set has been drawing since it was
# built and had nobody to draw it for.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 300

config
tab settings

# Down to Position and open it. The section's own rows first, so the two controls are on screen
# together before the heading separates them.
key down 5
key a
hold 900

# Into the group. Some of the set is ticked and some is not, which is what a checkbox column
# says at a glance and a column of "on"/"off" words does not.
key down 6
hold 1200

# Left and Right flip one, exactly as they flip a toggle - the mark grows rather than jumping,
# and the marker gutter picks up the dot that says this row is changed and not yet saved.
key right
hold 800
key down 1
hold 500
key right
hold 800
key left
hold 1200
